{"name":"Ashabenford","status":"ok","title":"Ashabenford","pageId":35057,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Ashabenford</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"aliases\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Aliases</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Ashabanford<sup id=\"cite_ref-cotab-p36_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-cotab-p36-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Settlement</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mistledale\" title=\"Mistledale\">Mistledale</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dalelands\" title=\"Dalelands\">Dalelands</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Small Town</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><table class=\"percentagetable\"><tbody><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a>  </td><td> 87%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarves\">Dwarves</a>  </td><td> 5%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">Gnomes</a>  </td><td> 3%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">Halflings</a>  </td><td> 2%  </td></tr><tr><td> <a href=\"/wiki/Half-elves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Half-elves\">Half-elves</a>  </td><td> 2% </td></tr><tr><td> Other </td><td> 1% </td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Chauntea\" title=\"Chauntea\">Chauntea</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, <a href=\"/wiki/Tyr\" title=\"Tyr\">Tyr</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ale\" title=\"Ale\">Ale</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Beets (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmVldHM/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">beets</span>, <a href=\"/wiki/Cheese\" title=\"Cheese\">cheese</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Grain (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR3JhaW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">grain</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Hay (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGF5P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">hay</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Meat (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWVhdD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">meat</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Potatoes (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUG90YXRvZXM/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">potatoes</span>, and other <span class=\"new\" title=\"Vegetables (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVmVnZXRhYmxlcz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">vegetables</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"government\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Republic with elected administrator<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"rulertype\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"High Councilor (Mistledale) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGlnaF9Db3VuY2lsb3JfKE1pc3RsZWRhbGUpP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">High Councilor</span></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">455<sup id=\"cite_ref-TD-p35_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TD-p35-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367&#160;DR</a><br>1,869&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"High Councilor (Mistledale) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGlnaF9Db3VuY2lsb3JfKE1pc3RsZWRhbGUpP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">High Councilor</span></h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Haresk_Malorn\" title=\"Haresk Malorn\">Haresk Malorn</a>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Ashabenford\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Ashabenford\">Inhabitants of  Ashabenford</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Ashabenford\" title=\"Category:Locations in Ashabenford\">Locations in  Ashabenford</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Ashabenford\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Ashabenford\">Organizations in  Ashabenford</a></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Ashabenford</b> was the capital and largest settlement of <a href=\"/wiki/Mistledale\" title=\"Mistledale\">Mistledale</a>, the central, most-well-protected dale within the <a href=\"/wiki/Dalelands\" title=\"Dalelands\">Dalelands</a>. It served as a marketplace for local Dalesfolk farmers and generally a pleasant locale for visitors.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Defenses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defenses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Homes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Homes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Inns_and_Boarding_Houses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inns and Boarding Houses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Shops_and_Costers\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Shops and Costers</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Taverns\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Taverns</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Temples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Temples</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Notable_Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gallery</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Composed of rustic homes and collections of cottages, Ashabenford sat on the eastern side of the <a href=\"/wiki/River_Ashaba\" title=\"River Ashaba\">River Ashaba</a>, though some of its notable buildings were found also on the west bank. The busy trade route of the <a href=\"/wiki/Moonsea_Ride\" title=\"Moonsea Ride\">Moonsea Ride</a> passed through the center of the small town,<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p179_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p179-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and it served as a major stop between <a href=\"/wiki/Cormyr\" title=\"Cormyr\">Cormyr</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Hillsfar\" title=\"Hillsfar\">Hillsfar</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TD-p36_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TD-p36-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Council_of_Six\" class=\"mw-disambig\" title=\"Council of Six\">Council of Six</a> were elected representatives from around Mistledale who appointed the <span class=\"new\" title=\"High Councilor (Mistledale) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGlnaF9Db3VuY2lsb3JfKE1pc3RsZWRhbGUpP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">High Councilor</span> of both Ashabenford and the dale. Once chosen, the High Councilor was expected to reside in Ashabenford all year round. Between, at least, the years of <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>, the reigning High Councilor was <a href=\"/wiki/Haresk_Malorn\" title=\"Haresk Malorn\">Haresk Malorn</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TD-p34_7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TD-p34-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The presence of the Moonsea Ride meant the town had little need for a large open air market, with many services instead being found along the route. Local farmers keen to sell their wares avoided the main trade route, tending instead to stop the wagons in the many yards or lanes dotted around the pleasant backstreets of the town.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p179_5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p179-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defenses\">Defenses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Defenses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Defenses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As the Barracks of the Riders was located in Ashabenford, the town was regularly garrisoned and patrolled by around sixteen <a href=\"/wiki/Riders_of_Mistledale\" title=\"Riders of Mistledale\">Riders of Mistledale</a>. In addition, between 50 or 60 militia members were kept there in training.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p181_8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p181-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Haresk%27s_Pool\" title=\"Haresk's Pool\">Haresk's Pool</a>: A pond near the <span class=\"new\" title=\"House of the High Councilor (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfdGhlX0hpZ2hfQ291bmNpbG9yP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">House of the High Councilor</span> that was rumored to contain an old bandit lord's cache of treasure at the bottom of its depths.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Horsewater_Pool\" title=\"Horsewater Pool\">Horsewater Pool</a>: This well was a literal watering hole for the local townsfolk to gather, share news and gossip.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Thorm%27s_Mill\" title=\"Thorm's Mill\">Thorm's Mill</a>: The only mill in Mistledale was run by the miserly <a href=\"/wiki/Thorm_Ubler\" title=\"Thorm Ubler\">Thorm Ubler</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Homes\">Homes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Homes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Homes\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Arvien%27s_Home\" title=\"Arvien's Home\">Arvien's Home</a>: The house of the town's <a href=\"/wiki/Tinsmith\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tinsmith\">tinsmith</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p183_9-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p183-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"House of the High Councilor (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfdGhlX0hpZ2hfQ291bmNpbG9yP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">House of the High Councilor</span>: The largest house in Mistledale served as both home to the High Chancillor and the seat of power for the Council of Six.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Jhaer_Brightsong\" title=\"Jhaer Brightsong\">Jhaer Brightsong</a>'s house: This was the home of Mistledale's famous traveling minstrel.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Noristuor\" title=\"Noristuor\">Noristuor</a>'s residence: Home to the frightening and disliked <a href=\"/wiki/Mage\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mage\">mage</a> who recently moved to Ashabenford.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inns_and_Boarding_Houses\">Inns and Boarding Houses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Inns and Boarding Houses\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=7\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Inns and Boarding Houses\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Ashabenford_Arms\" title=\"Ashabenford Arms\">Ashabenford Arms</a>: An excellent inn with unequaled rooms and service.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Barracks of the <a href=\"/wiki/Riders_of_Mistledale\" title=\"Riders of Mistledale\">Riders</a>: This walled hold was home to Mistledale's first-line defenders. It housed their training grounds, as a small keep used as the dale's jailhouse.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/The_Six_Shields\" title=\"The Six Shields\">The Six Shields</a>: A rooming house that offered room and board to the dales working people for low cost.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p187_10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p187-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/White_Hart_Inn\" title=\"White Hart Inn\">White Hart Inn</a>: This honest inn, run by <a href=\"/wiki/Holfast_Harpenshield\" title=\"Holfast Harpenshield\">Holfast Harpenshield</a>, catered to adventurers and had very reasonable rates.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shops_and_Costers\">Shops and Costers</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Shops and Costers\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=8\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Shops and Costers\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Almaes_the_Alchemist%27s_shop\" title=\"Almaes the Alchemist's shop\">Almaes the Alchemist's shop</a>: The <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">gnome</a> Alames, or more properly <a href=\"/wiki/Almaestaddamir_Auldcastle\" title=\"Almaestaddamir Auldcastle\">Almaestaddamir Auldcastle</a>, offered a variety of alchemical mixtures including <a href=\"/wiki/Smokepowder\" title=\"Smokepowder\">smokepowder</a>, various <a href=\"/wiki/Acid\" title=\"Acid\">acids</a>, antitoxins and the like.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Braunstar_Wheelwright\" title=\"Braunstar Wheelwright\">Braunstar Wheelwright</a>: The proprietor of this wagon shop, the wise Dalesman <a href=\"/wiki/Braunstar\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Braunstar\">Braunstar</a>, provided all kinds of services related to his craft.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Black_Eagle_Coster\" title=\"Black Eagle Coster\">Black Eagle Coster</a>: This company bought local goods from merchants and farmers, and sold them to <a href=\"/wiki/Hillsfar\" title=\"Hillsfar\">Hillsfar</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Harrowdale\" title=\"Harrowdale\">Harrowdale</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Haresk%27s_Hardware_Emporium\" title=\"Haresk's Hardware Emporium\">Haresk's Hardware Emporium</a>: An old, cluttered general store owned by the town's High Councilor.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p184_11-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p184-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Jarwain%27s_Imports\" title=\"Jarwain's Imports\">Jarwain's Imports</a>: A small store that specialized in silk, <a href=\"/wiki/Spices\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Spices\">spices</a>. cotton and other luxury goods from Cormyr.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Kaulvaeras_Stables\" title=\"Kaulvaeras Stables\">Kaulvaeras Stables</a>: One of the finer stables within the Dalelands, <a href=\"/wiki/Kaulvaeras_Greymantle\" title=\"Kaulvaeras Greymantle\">Kaulvaeras Greymantle</a> offered a fine selection of ponies, horses and warhorses.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Lhuin%27s_Fine_Leathers\" title=\"Lhuin's Fine Leathers\">Lhuin's Fine Leathers</a>: This shop provided outstanding work at significantly discounted prices.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-11\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Multhimmer_the_Merchant%27s_shop\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Multhimmer the Merchant's shop\">Multhimmer the Merchant's shop</a>: A fine trading post that would occasionally sell stolen goods but never buy them as a fence.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-12\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Taverns\">Taverns</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Taverns\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=9\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Taverns\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Arlho%27s_Fine_Flasks\" title=\"Arlho's Fine Flasks\">Arlho's Fine Flasks</a>: Run by a sheepish <a href=\"/wiki/Cormyrian\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cormyrian\">Cormyrian</a>, this brewery/distillery sold goods of excellent quality. Rhynn Oriandis and his longstanding ally, Jander Sunstar, would frequent this spot for ale quite often. <sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-13\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Velvet_Veil\" title=\"Velvet Veil\">Velvet Veil</a>: Rumors and stories from all the corners of <a href=\"/wiki/Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Faerûn\">Faerûn</a> came through this festhall and was regularly shared by the local entertainers and serving staff.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Temples\">Temples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Temples\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=10\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Temples\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Harvest Table (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGFydmVzdF9UYWJsZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Harvest Table</span>: This small, roadside shrine to the <i>Great Mother</i> was popular among the locals,<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p181-2_12-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p181-2-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> but dwarfed by the massive temple of <a href=\"/wiki/Tyr\" title=\"Tyr\">Tyr</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p134_3-14\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p134-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Temple of Tyr (Ashabenford) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGVtcGxlX29mX1R5cl8oQXNoYWJlbmZvcmQpP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Temple of Tyr</span>: The clergy of this grand sanctuary aided the Riders of Mistledale in their defense of Cormanthor against the Drow.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p133_2-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p133-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Inhabitants\">Notable Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=11\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Darhlas\" title=\"Darhlas\">Darhlas</a>, a <a href=\"/wiki/Blacksmith\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Blacksmith\">blacksmith</a> inhabiting Ashabenford during the mid-to-late 14<sup>th</sup> century DR.<sup id=\"cite_ref-IA_13-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-IA-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Iletian_Blackeagle\" title=\"Iletian Blackeagle\">Iletian Blackeagle</a>, former adventurer, craft brewer, and owner of Black Eagle Coster.<sup id=\"cite_ref-VGtD-p183_9-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-VGtD-p183-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tanlatha_Tyrlan\" title=\"Tanlatha Tyrlan\">Tanlatha Tyrlan</a>, a farmer inhabiting the town of Ashabenford in the mid-to-late 14<sup>th</sup> century DR.<sup id=\"cite_ref-IA_13-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-IA-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=12\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Gallery\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=13\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Gallery\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"f6bfd105b5c889820f97e00c72f3aad6\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=14\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Video Games</dt>\n<dd><i><a href=\"/wiki/Curse_of_the_Azure_Bonds_(game)\" title=\"Curse of the Azure Bonds (game)\">Curse of the Azure Bonds</a></i></dd>\n<dd><b><small>Referenced only</small></b></dd>\n<dd><small><i><a href=\"/wiki/Baldur%27s_Gate_(game)\" title=\"Baldur's Gate (game)\">Baldur's Gate</a></i></small></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ashabenford?veaction=edit&section=15\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-cotab-p36-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-cotab-p36_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Grubb\" title=\"Jeff Grubb\">Jeff Grubb</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/George_MacDonald\" title=\"George Mac